    {
      "id": "1569324889587064952",
      "type": "Default",
      "timestamp": "2026-11-09T12:16:50.324+00:00",
      "timestampEdited": null,
      "callEndedTimestamp": null,
      "isPinned": false,
      "content": "✅ mattvenn reported @algofoogle (Anton Maurovic)'s [Ring osc on VGA](https://www.tinytapeout.com/chips/ttgf0p2/tt_um_algofoogle_vgaringosc) as working: The rings run from 23.7 MHz (161 stages) to 220.5 MHz (3 stages); the fixed 5× inv_1 ring runs at about 320 MHz. \n\nPeriod fits T = 0.240 ns × N + 4.19 ns: about 120 ps per inv_2 stage (T = 2·N·t_pd) plus about 4.2 ns fixed loop overhead (tap multiplexer and clock buffer). \n\nuio[1] (clksel2[1]) wasn't working so we couldn't test the 5 × inv_4 ring",
      "author": {
        "id": "1167741026950197258",
        "name": "TTBot",
        "discriminator": "6027",
        "nickname": "TTBot",
        "color": null,
        "isBot": true,
        "roles": [
